{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find the current official Scalable Press API v2 documentation for test mode/sandbox, authentication, creating a DTG design by uploading artwork, creating a quote, and placing an order. Include exact endpoints, current request field names, response shapes, and how test API keys behave. Focus on docs.scalablepress.com and official sources."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find the current official Scalable Press API v2 documentation for test mode/sandbox, authentication, creating a DTG design by uploading artwork, creating a quote, and placing an order. Include exact endpoints, current request field names, response shapes, and how test API keys behave. Focus on docs.scalablepress.com and official sources."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Scalable Press API v2 Documentation\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe Scalable Press API v2 documentation provides comprehensive guidelines on authentication, utilizing test mode, uploading artwork for Direct-to-Garment (DTG) designs, creating quotes, and placing orders. It details specific endpoints, request parameters, response structures, and the behavior of test API keys to facilitate seamless integration.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** Authentication requires an API key, which must be included in the request header as `Authorization: Bearer {API_KEY}`.\n\n- **Finding 2:** Test mode is enabled by appending `?test=true` to API requests, allowing developers to simulate transactions without actual charges.\n\n- **Finding 3:** To create a DTG design, send a POST request to `/v2/designs` with parameters including `type`, `name`, and `files` containing the artwork URL.\n\n- **Finding 4:** Quotes are generated by POSTing to `/v2/quotes` with details like `designId`, `products`, and `address`, returning pricing information.\n\n- **Finding 5:** Orders are placed via a POST request to `/v2/orders` with parameters such as `quoteId` and `payment`, initiating the fulfillment process.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: Scalable Press API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** [https://docs.scalablepress.com](https://docs.scalablepress.com)\n\n- **Domain:** docs.scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official source from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press API documentation outlines the procedures for authenticating API requests, operating in test mode, creating DTG designs by uploading artwork, generating quotes, and placing orders. It specifies the necessary endpoints, request parameters, and response formats to assist developers in integrating with the Scalable Press platform.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- **Authentication:** API key required in header as `Authorization: Bearer {API_KEY}`.\n\n- **Test Mode:** Enabled by adding `?test=true` to API requests.\n\n- **Design Creation Endpoint:** POST `/v2/designs` with parameters `type`, `name`, and `files` containing artwork URL.\n\n- **Quote Generation Endpoint:** POST `/v2/quotes` with `designId`, `products`, and `address`.\n\n- **Order Placement Endpoint:** POST `/v2/orders` with `quoteId` and `payment`.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"To authenticate API requests, include your API key in the request header as `Authorization: Bearer {API_KEY}`.\"\n\n> \"Test mode can be activated by appending `?test=true` to your API requests, allowing you to simulate transactions without actual charges.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- Authentication requires including the API key in the request header as `Authorization: Bearer {API_KEY}`.\n\n- Test mode is activated by appending `?test=true` to API requests.\n\n- Endpoints for creating designs, generating quotes, and placing orders are `/v2/designs`, `/v2/quotes`, and `/v2/orders` respectively.\n\n**Conflicting Information:**\n\n- No conflicting information identified across sources.\n\n**Information Gaps:**\n\n- Specific details on response structures and example payloads for each endpoint are not provided in the available documentation.\n\n- Behavior of test API keys in scenarios involving payment processing is not explicitly detailed.\n\n---\n\n## Research Metadata\n\n- **Search Completed:** 2026-08-23T20:22:05Z\n\n- **Sources Analyzed:** 1 source\n\n- **Total Content Reviewed:** Approximately 1,500 words\n\n- **Search Confidence:** Medium (Limited to a single official source)\n\n--- "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"5b8713fe-24e5-4c36-af62-998006a7dc3f"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
