{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Search GitHub and the web for real working code examples of POST https://api.scalablepress.com/v2/quote, especially DTG products and the exact address JSON field names. Also find current Scalable Press API v2 quote docs or npm SDK implementation. Return verbatim request examples and source URLs. Do not infer plural v3 endpoints."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Search GitHub and the web for real working code examples of POST https://api.scalablepress.com/v2/quote, especially DTG products and the exact address JSON field names. Also find current Scalable Press API v2 quote docs or npm SDK implementation. Return verbatim request examples and source URLs. Do not infer plural v3 endpoints."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: POST https://api.scalablepress.com/v2/quote\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe Scalable Press API v2 provides a `POST` endpoint at `https://api.scalablepress.com/v2/quote` for obtaining quotes on direct-to-garment (DTG) products. To generate an order-ready quote, the request must include product details, a design ID, and a complete shipping address. The API documentation offers detailed examples and specifies the required JSON field names for the address.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** An order-ready quote requires the `type` set to `dtg`, product details (`id`, `color`, `quantity`, `size`), a valid `designId`, and a complete `address` object.\n\n- **Finding 2:** The `address` object must include the fields: `name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, and `zip`.\n\n- **Finding 3:** Authentication is performed using HTTP Basic Auth, with the API key as the password and the username left blank.\n\n- **Finding 4:** The API provides different outcomes: `order-ready` for complete information, `quote-only` when some information is missing, and `error` for invalid or incomplete data.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** https://scalablepress.com/docs/\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official source from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press API documentation outlines the process for obtaining quotes via the `POST /v2/quote` endpoint. It specifies that for an order-ready quote, the request must include the `type` set to `dtg`, product details such as `id`, `color`, `quantity`, and `size`, a valid `designId`, and a complete `address` object. The `address` object should contain `name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, and `zip`. Authentication is performed using HTTP Basic Auth, with the API key as the password and the username left blank. The API returns different outcomes based on the completeness and validity of the provided information: `order-ready`, `quote-only`, or `error`.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Required `address` fields: `name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, `zip`\n\n- Authentication: HTTP Basic Auth with API key as password\n\n- Possible outcomes: `order-ready`, `quote-only`, `error`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"An order-ready quote requires the `type` set to `dtg`, product details, a valid `designId`, and a complete `address` object.\"\n\n> \"The `address` object must include the fields: `name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, and `zip`.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- The requirement for a complete `address` object with specific fields (`name`, `address1`, `city`, `state`, `zip`) is consistently emphasized across sources.\n\n- Authentication via HTTP Basic Auth, using the API key as the password, is a standard practice noted in the documentation.\n\n**Conflicting Information:**\n\n- No conflicting information was identified among the sources.\n\n**Information Gaps:**\n\n- The documentation does not provide explicit examples of error responses for invalid or incomplete data.\n\n- Details on handling bulk quotes or multiple designs are not extensively covered.\n\n---\n\n## Research Metadata\n\n- **Search Completed:** 2026-08-23T20:39:50Z\n\n- **Sources Analyzed:** 1 source\n\n- **Total Content Reviewed:** Approximately 500 words\n\n- **Search Confidence:** High (Based on official documentation)\n\n---\n\n**Verbatim Request Example:**\n\n```bash\ncurl \"https://api.scalablepress.com/v2/quote\" \\\n  -u \"<YOUR_API_KEY>:\" \\\n  -d \"type=dtg\" \\\n  -d \"products[0][id]=gildan-sweatshirt-crew\" \\\n  -d \"products[0][color]=ash\" \\\n  -d \"products[0][quantity]=12\" \\\n  -d \"products[0][size]=lrg\" \\\n  -d \"address[name]=My Customer\" \\\n  -d \"address[address1]=123 Scalable Drive\" \\\n  -d \"address[city]=West Pressfield\" \\\n  -d \"address[state]=CA\" \\\n  -d \"address[zip]=12345\" \\\n  -d \"designId=53ed3a23b3730f0e27a66513\"\n```\n\n**Source URL:** https://scalablepress.com/docs/ "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"9d92fa9e-8239-4518-8141-8214f7527048"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
